  "response": "3개월이면 꽤 오래 버텨오신 건데, 게다가 점점 더 길어지고 있다니 더 지치셨을 것 같아요.\n\n잠이 안 올 때 그 시간 동안은 주로 어떤 상태예요? 머릿속으로 여러 생각이 계속 맴도는지, 아니면 몸이 불편하거나 긴장되는 느낌이 있는지요.",
  "reasoning": "The user is a counselor responding to a client. The client has shared that they've had insomnia for about 3 months, taking 1-2 hours to fall asleep, and lately it's taking even longer. \n\nI need to respond as a counselor in Korean. I should:\n- Acknowledge what they've shared\n- Show understanding of the difficulty (3 months is a significant period, and it's getting worse)\n- Not rush to solutions or minimize\n- Ask one relevant question to understand the situation better, or offer a helpful direction\n\nWhat would be helpful here? The client has given me duration (3 months), severity (1-2 hours to fall asleep, worsening). I could:\n1. Acknowledge the worsening trend and the toll of 3 months\n2. Ask about what happens during those hours of not sleeping - is it rumination, anxiety, physical restlessness? This would help understand the nature of the insomnia.\n\nI think acknowledging the worsening and asking what's happening during those hours would be natural and helpful. It opens up understanding whether this is anxiety-driven, rumination, or something else.\n",
  "started_at": "2026-10-31T04:14:57.643875+00:00",
